# Rank 1175 / CVE-2022-41137: Apache Hive's metastore Thrift server
# deserializes a partition-filter expression with Kryo and no restriction on
# which classes may come back. HMSHandler.get_partitions_by_expr (Thrift
# service method, `implements ThriftHiveMetastore.Iface`) hands the request's
# raw `exprBytes` to PartitionExpressionForMetastore.filterPartitionsByExpr,
# which calls deserializeExpr, which calls
# SerializationUtilities.deserializeObjectWithTypeInformation(bytes) --
# `kryo.readClassAndObject(inp)` on the caller-supplied bytes, unregistered,
# so any class on the classpath can be the object Kryo builds (CWE-502): a
# client with metastore access can hand get_partitions_by_expr a gadget-chain
# payload instead of a serialized ExprNodeDesc.
#
# The fixed revision does not stop calling
# readClassAndObject on the raw bytes -- it adds a class allowlist at the
# point Kryo resolves each class. SerializationUtilities.KryoWithHooks (a
# private static nested Kryo subclass) overrides Kryo's own extension point
# `getRegistration(Class type)`; when a new `isExprNodeFirst` flag is set,
# the first class the deserializer resolves must be assignable from
# ExprNodeDesc or the override throws UnsupportedOperationException.
# deserializeObjectWithTypeInformation gained an `isPartFilter` parameter,
# and PartitionExpressionForMetastore.deserializeExpr now passes `true`,
# arming the check before readClassAndObject runs.
#
# Two independent gaps, diagnosed with `vyql match` on a reduced repro of
# both revisions (neither labels anything):
#
# 1. Sink, fixed here: the shipped binding for readClassAndObject
#    (vyql/bindings/packages/generated/java/com.esotericsoftware_kryo.vyql,
#    deserialization2) gates on dependency("com.esotericsoftware:kryo").
#    That gate can never open for Java: internal/extract/sca/discover.go's
#    manifest table has no pom.xml or build.gradle reader, so no Java
#    project's Kryo dependency is ever recorded, confirmed by adding a
#    pom.xml declaring the dependency to the repro and re-running `vyql
#    match` -- still nothing. readClassAndObject is Kryo's own method name,
#    not shared with an unrelated API, so binding deserialization762 in
#    vyql/bindings/java/m420f6b67.vyql drops the gate, mirroring
#    deserialization129/130 immediately above it (readObject/readUnshared,
#    already ungated for the same reason).
#
# 2. Source, not fixed here: nothing labels a Thrift service method's
#    parameters as network-controlled. `implements *.Iface` is Thrift's own
#    generated marker for "this class receives requests over the wire," a
#    generic pattern with no library-specific judgement, but adding it here
#    is not enough by itself -- see below.
#
# Shipping both a source and the sink fix together would make VYQL-DESER-001
# fire on the fixed revision too, because the taint dataflow from exprBytes
# to readClassAndObject is identical at both revisions; the
# neutralizing control is not a call on the tainted value, it is a class
# check that runs later, inside KryoWithHooks.getRegistration, arming a
# nested Kryo subclass that deserializeExpr's caller never touches
# directly. core.SafeDeserialization has no Java binding for that shape, and
# the two candidate ways to add one both fail the genericity test:
#   - keying on `setExprNodeFirst`/`isPartFilter` names Hive's own method,
#     invented for this patch, not a Kryo API -- the definition of a
#     repro-shaped binding.
#   - keying on a `getRegistration` override structurally (a real, public
#     Kryo extension point) needs to relate that override, declared in
#     KryoWithHooks, to a readClassAndObject call in the enclosing
#     SerializationUtilities class. presenceNode's class-scope context
#     aggregates only the direct class body (internal/extract/lowering/
#     lowering.go's classMemberContextTokens explicitly excludes nested
#     classes), so a class-scope check keyed on
#     `node.context.functionName contains "getRegistration"` at
#     SerializationUtilities never sees KryoWithHooks's override -- it
#     would fire on the fixed file exactly as it fires on the vulnerable
#     one. Distinguishing them needs an object-identity relationship (this
#     specific Kryo instance is configured by that override ahead of this
#     specific readClassAndObject call), which is a dataflow relation the
#     binding layer's structural matching does not express.
#
# So the source binding stays unshipped rather than pair with the sink fix
# to produce a rule that cannot tell the two revisions apart. Both cases
# below assert reject on the real Hive shapes, pinning that today's state
# (post sink-fix) is silence on both, not false coverage on either. The
# sink fix's own effect is proven separately, against an already-covered
# source, in the two regression cases at the end.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-missing-control-concept

test "rank1175: vulnerable Hive PartitionExpressionForMetastore reaches Kryo readClassAndObject with no class check"
  lang java
  file org/apache/hadoop/hive/metastore/HMSHandler.java
  reject VYQL-DESER-001
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.hadoop.hive.metastore;

  public class HMSHandler implements ThriftHiveMetastore.Iface {
    private PartitionExpressionProxy expressionProxy;

    @Override
    public PartitionsByExprResult get_partitions_by_expr(PartitionsByExprRequest req) throws MetaException {
      byte[] exprBytes = req.getExpr();
      boolean hasUnknown = expressionProxy.filterPartitionsByExpr(
          req.getPartColumns(), exprBytes, req.getDefaultPartitionName(), new ArrayList<String>());
      return new PartitionsByExprResult(hasUnknown);
    }
  }
  ```
  file org/apache/hadoop/hive/ql/optimizer/ppr/PartitionExpressionForMetastore.java
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.hadoop.hive.ql.optimizer.ppr;

  import org.apache.hadoop.hive.metastore.api.MetaException;
  import org.apache.hadoop.hive.ql.exec.SerializationUtilities;
  import org.apache.hadoop.hive.ql.plan.ExprNodeDesc;

  public class PartitionExpressionForMetastore implements PartitionExpressionProxy {

    public boolean filterPartitionsByExpr(List<FieldSchema> partColumns, byte[] exprBytes,
        String defaultPartitionName, List<String> partitionNames) throws MetaException {
      ExprNodeDesc expr = deserializeExpr(exprBytes);
      return PartitionPruner.prunePartitionNames(partColumns, expr, defaultPartitionName, partitionNames);
    }

    private ExprNodeDesc deserializeExpr(byte[] exprBytes) throws MetaException {
      ExprNodeDesc expr = null;
      try {
        expr = SerializationUtilities.deserializeObjectWithTypeInformation(exprBytes);
      } catch (Exception ex) {
        throw new MetaException(ex.getMessage());
      }
      if (expr == null) {
        throw new MetaException("Failed to deserialize expression - ExprNodeDesc not present");
      }
      return expr;
    }
  }
  ```
  file org/apache/hadoop/hive/ql/exec/SerializationUtilities.java
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.hadoop.hive.ql.exec;

  import com.esotericsoftware.kryo.Kryo;
  import com.esotericsoftware.kryo.io.Input;
  import java.io.ByteArrayInputStream;

  public class SerializationUtilities {

    public static <T> T deserializeObjectWithTypeInformation(byte[] bytes) {
      Kryo kryo = borrowKryo();
      try (Input inp = new Input(new ByteArrayInputStream(bytes))) {
        return (T) kryo.readClassAndObject(inp);
      } finally {
        releaseKryo(kryo);
      }
    }

    public static Kryo borrowKryo() {
      return new Kryo();
    }

    public static void releaseKryo(Kryo kryo) {
    }
  }
  ```

